speechtext:
Most of them are, but there are a few who are exceptions or who use up too much of their time doing something else to be really good farmers. But the fact of the matter is that these farmers are getting a certain income and we should indicate that they are getting it. Because income is down $400 million in the three western provinces because of wheat, we should not come out and say that everybody else is suffering, that as a result of that every other farmer is suffering. It is all very well to say that the implement dealer is suffering as a result of not being able to sell so many implements;

Supply-Agriculture
it is all very well to say that others are suffering, that people in business are suffering; but to say that the farmers down in Nova Scotia or Quebec or Ontario are suffering because the returns for wheat are down $400 million is going a little too far.
